1
00:00:07,785 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,225 --> 00:01:39,025
ADAPTED FROM THE EARLY SPRING ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:43,625 --> 00:01:45,025
Stay. Sit.

4
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:54,945
Your silly master is calling.

5
00:01:58,625 --> 00:02:00,025
-Hello?
-Hello.

6
00:02:00,545 --> 00:02:02,025
Tracy said…

7
00:02:02,105 --> 00:02:02,985
What's wrong with your voice?

8
00:02:04,025 --> 00:02:05,265
Getting all emotional?

9
00:02:06,985 --> 00:02:07,825
No.

10
00:02:08,665 --> 00:02:10,385
I'm calling to thank you.

11
00:02:11,945 --> 00:02:13,025
It was nothing.

12
00:02:14,345 --> 00:02:15,265
How are you going to thank me?

13
00:02:17,505 --> 00:02:19,145
I'll buy you dinner.

14
00:02:19,985 --> 00:02:21,105
When?

15
00:02:21,865 --> 00:02:22,785
Tomorrow.

16
00:02:24,745 --> 00:02:25,985
What are you up to today?

17
00:02:26,625 --> 00:02:30,625
I promised to help Sun Yu
with her first startup event.

18
00:02:33,465 --> 00:02:34,425
Alright.

19
00:02:53,705 --> 00:02:57,665
BUCKET LIST

20
00:03:05,785 --> 00:03:08,145
MY HEART WAITS ONLY FOR YOU

21
00:03:13,025 --> 00:03:14,185
Please sign here.

22
00:03:18,025 --> 00:03:19,705
Drink this. I'm good.

23
00:03:20,305 --> 00:03:22,545
It's a relief having you here.
I'm swamped inside.

24
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:24,345
Don't worry. I've got
things covered out here.

25
00:03:25,265 --> 00:03:26,225
I'll leave this to you.

26
00:03:26,305 --> 00:03:28,025
-Go on.
-I'm going.

27
00:03:28,785 --> 00:03:29,705
Sign here.

28
00:03:30,545 --> 00:03:31,705
-This way.
-Sign here, right?

29
00:03:31,785 --> 00:03:33,585
Yeah. Here. This way.

30
00:03:33,665 --> 00:03:34,505
Number 13.

31
00:03:34,585 --> 00:03:35,585
Hello, miss.

32
00:03:35,665 --> 00:03:36,945
Mind if I get to know you?

33
00:03:37,025 --> 00:03:39,545
There are lots of great members inside.

34
00:03:39,625 --> 00:03:41,505
You can go in and meet people.

35
00:03:42,505 --> 00:03:43,945
What's your number?

36
00:03:44,025 --> 00:03:45,145
May I get to know you?

37
00:03:46,945 --> 00:03:47,985
You can head in first.

38
00:03:48,065 --> 00:03:49,745
There'll be plenty of people
to welcome you.

39
00:03:50,265 --> 00:03:52,545
-Alright.
-Please fill in detals, Sir.

40
00:03:52,625 --> 00:03:53,865
‎Thank you.

41
00:03:55,985 --> 00:03:57,065
This way, please.

42
00:03:57,625 --> 00:03:58,465
‎Thank you.

43
00:04:00,145 --> 00:04:01,105
-Keep an eye on things for me.
-Okay.

44
00:04:01,185 --> 00:04:02,865
-Give me one of those.
-Alright.

45
00:04:10,745 --> 00:04:12,025
Are you here for the matchmaking?

46
00:04:12,625 --> 00:04:15,105
You put on makeup and dressed up nicely.

47
00:04:18,305 --> 00:04:19,745
What are you doing here?

48
00:04:20,905 --> 00:04:22,705
I came to check out the investment project
I recommended,

49
00:04:23,225 --> 00:04:24,705
only to find out it was a dating scam.

50
00:04:26,065 --> 00:04:28,545
Don't put it that way.
It's not a dating scam.

51
00:04:29,785 --> 00:04:33,305
Sun Yu is organizing
a normal singles networking event.

52
00:04:34,545 --> 00:04:35,625
Tao Zhi Yao Yao.

53
00:04:37,265 --> 00:04:39,625
Graduated from Penn.
Works for a foreign company.

54
00:04:39,705 --> 00:04:40,545
Four hundred thousand a year.

55
00:04:41,265 --> 00:04:43,305
171 centimeters tall. 54 kilograms.

56
00:04:43,385 --> 00:04:46,145
Enjoys skiing, diving, and golf.

57
00:04:46,945 --> 00:04:48,465
Fluent in three languages.

58
00:04:49,065 --> 00:04:51,425
Luan Nian, the profile
was computer-generated.

59
00:04:51,505 --> 00:04:53,705
You know that.
I can't do any of those sports.

60
00:04:55,225 --> 00:04:57,625
This account has chatted with 45 members.

61
00:04:59,105 --> 00:05:00,505
So when you said
you were busy during weekends,

62
00:05:02,145 --> 00:05:04,945
you were actually here
pretending to date people?

63
00:05:08,705 --> 00:05:10,505
Those accounts are all managed
by the company.

64
00:05:10,585 --> 00:05:12,345
I've never logged into it.

65
00:05:12,425 --> 00:05:14,065
Then that proves this app is a scam.

66
00:05:14,905 --> 00:05:15,865
I'm stopping the investment.

67
00:05:16,465 --> 00:05:18,945
I'll notify the investors
and reassess these risks.

68
00:05:19,025 --> 00:05:20,065
Don't.

69
00:05:20,145 --> 00:05:21,945
Don't drag Sun Yu into this because of me.

70
00:05:22,025 --> 00:05:24,665
She's still in the startup stage.
It hasn't been easy for her.

71
00:05:24,745 --> 00:05:26,385
Don't stop the investment.

72
00:05:27,505 --> 00:05:28,705
Then get another investor,

73
00:05:29,385 --> 00:05:30,585
so she can get money sooner

74
00:05:30,665 --> 00:05:34,545
and hire more actors
for these dating scam events.

75
00:05:45,105 --> 00:05:46,105
Don't take me for a fool.

76
00:06:11,585 --> 00:06:13,265
ARE YOU SURE YOU WANT
TO DELETE YOUR ACCOUNT?

77
00:06:13,345 --> 00:06:14,185
DELETE ACCOUNT

78
00:06:29,025 --> 00:06:31,665
Very well. Dating scams are cheap.

79
00:06:31,745 --> 00:06:34,625
Even if you're just a shill,
it's nothing to be proud of.

80
00:06:57,505 --> 00:07:00,105
-My back is killing me.
-Come here, Luke.

81
00:07:00,185 --> 00:07:01,825
I'm exhausted. I'm going to lie down.

82
00:07:01,905 --> 00:07:02,865
Luke.

83
00:07:04,425 --> 00:07:05,665
You're back.

84
00:07:06,345 --> 00:07:07,785
Why are you home?

85
00:07:09,905 --> 00:07:11,065
Smells great.

86
00:07:11,145 --> 00:07:12,425
You started cooking once you got home?

87
00:07:14,305 --> 00:07:15,585
You've lost weight again.

88
00:07:15,665 --> 00:07:16,985
Did you skip your meals?

89
00:07:17,985 --> 00:07:18,865
I didn't.

90
00:07:18,945 --> 00:07:21,025
It's probably because
I've been busy with the experiments.

91
00:07:22,225 --> 00:07:24,185
I have been eating lots of meat.

92
00:07:24,265 --> 00:07:25,785
I brought back some Tan sheep.

93
00:07:26,625 --> 00:07:28,385
We'll grill lamb tonight.

94
00:07:28,465 --> 00:07:29,945
I'll take Luke to eat first.

95
00:07:30,745 --> 00:07:31,705
Go on, Luke.

96
00:07:31,785 --> 00:07:32,905
-Luke.
-See what you have for dinner.

97
00:07:34,585 --> 00:07:35,745
Come here.

98
00:07:44,625 --> 00:07:46,145
What's wrong?

99
00:07:46,225 --> 00:07:47,505
Stop looking at me.

100
00:07:49,705 --> 00:07:52,385
I'll make Yuanzhu some millet porridge.
It's good for his stomach.

101
00:07:54,425 --> 00:07:56,345
You're making him millet porridge?

102
00:07:57,265 --> 00:07:58,665
Putting a man before your friend, huh?

103
00:07:59,985 --> 00:08:01,025
Shut up.

104
00:08:05,785 --> 00:08:07,105
You deleted the account.

105
00:08:07,185 --> 00:08:08,385
Is Luan Nian still mad at you?

106
00:08:12,425 --> 00:08:14,105
I don't know. Whatever.

107
00:08:16,505 --> 00:08:20,065
The fact that he cared so much
means he really cares about you.

108
00:08:20,145 --> 00:08:20,985
It's on me.

109
00:08:22,305 --> 00:08:24,545
I didn't know
they were using your account.

110
00:08:24,625 --> 00:08:27,105
Otherwise, you two wouldn't have fought.

111
00:08:27,905 --> 00:08:29,425
I've told them to fix it.

112
00:08:30,305 --> 00:08:32,345
I don't want Luan Nian
to misunderstand you.

113
00:08:32,425 --> 00:08:33,585
I'd feel terrible about it.

114
00:08:34,264 --> 00:08:35,545
Besides, he helped me find investors.

115
00:08:35,625 --> 00:08:37,865
-You two--
-Don't overthink it.

116
00:08:38,945 --> 00:08:39,784
Okay?

117
00:08:39,865 --> 00:08:41,264
Don't worry.

118
00:08:41,345 --> 00:08:42,185
I can handle it.

119
00:08:44,825 --> 00:08:47,865
I'm starting to think workplace
relationships are just like romantic ones.

120
00:08:48,905 --> 00:08:51,705
If the other person doesn't trust you,
nothing you say will matter.

121
00:08:55,585 --> 00:08:59,025
Tao, do you see Luan Nian
as your boyfriend

122
00:08:59,905 --> 00:09:01,345
or your boss?

123
00:09:09,905 --> 00:09:11,225
I can't tell anymore.

124
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:15,545
Maybe

125
00:09:16,545 --> 00:09:18,905
before I can see anyone as an equal,

126
00:09:20,345 --> 00:09:22,465
every relationship has someone above
and someone below.

127
00:09:25,785 --> 00:09:28,585
Tao dear, you sound a lot more mature now.

128
00:09:29,185 --> 00:09:32,185
Likewise. Now get back to cooking,

129
00:09:32,265 --> 00:09:33,545
Miss Sun.

130
00:09:34,625 --> 00:09:35,985
ONE MONTH LATER

131
00:09:36,065 --> 00:09:38,545
I'll meet up with the client first
in Shenzhen,

132
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:39,905
then let's meet, okay?

133
00:09:41,305 --> 00:09:42,585
No problem.

134
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:44,345
I've taken annual leave.

135
00:09:44,425 --> 00:09:46,545
When you get here, I'll show you around.

136
00:09:49,305 --> 00:09:50,025
YAO BEI

137
00:09:50,105 --> 00:09:51,545
You're coming to Shenzhen for work.

138
00:09:51,625 --> 00:09:53,385
Let's meet. Xin Zhaozhou.

139
00:09:54,825 --> 00:09:57,265
Bei, is Xin Zhaozhou in Shenzhen too?

140
00:09:57,345 --> 00:09:59,985
He just texted me.
He said he'd like to see me.

141
00:10:01,425 --> 00:10:03,785
I told him you were coming to Shenzhen
on business.

142
00:10:03,865 --> 00:10:06,625
I heard he received a government grant

143
00:10:06,705 --> 00:10:09,585
and started a trading company there.

144
00:10:09,665 --> 00:10:11,785
He's a big shot now.

145
00:10:14,185 --> 00:10:15,185
Would you like to see him?

146
00:10:15,985 --> 00:10:17,305
Why wouldn't I?

147
00:10:17,385 --> 00:10:18,465
It's not like we're enemies.

148
00:10:18,545 --> 00:10:20,185
We parted on good terms.

149
00:10:20,265 --> 00:10:24,425
After all, we shared the best years
of our lives together.

150
00:10:25,145 --> 00:10:27,385
Do you think he's still not over you

151
00:10:27,465 --> 00:10:28,625
and trying to get back together?

152
00:10:30,825 --> 00:10:31,705
No way.

153
00:10:31,785 --> 00:10:33,505
Even if he wanted to, I wouldn't.

154
00:10:33,585 --> 00:10:34,905
Don't overthink it.

155
00:10:36,545 --> 00:10:38,185
Alright. We'll talk later.

156
00:10:45,985 --> 00:10:49,345
SHENZHEN

157
00:10:55,945 --> 00:10:56,825
Luke,

158
00:10:56,905 --> 00:10:59,265
if we don't have dinner plans tonight,
I'll head out on my own.

159
00:10:59,345 --> 00:11:00,465
I'm meeting a friend.

160
00:11:01,225 --> 00:11:02,265
A friend?

161
00:11:03,465 --> 00:11:04,545
My college classmate.

162
00:11:05,585 --> 00:11:06,585
He's also my ex-boyfriend.

163
00:11:07,665 --> 00:11:08,905
Shang Zhitao.

164
00:11:33,945 --> 00:11:35,625
You're early.

165
00:11:42,385 --> 00:11:43,385
Is this your colleague?

166
00:11:45,385 --> 00:11:47,425
This is… This is my boss, Luke.

167
00:11:48,385 --> 00:11:51,745
This is my friend, Xin Zhaozhou.

168
00:11:51,825 --> 00:11:53,225
We're having dinner tonight.

169
00:12:00,265 --> 00:12:01,145
Have a good catch-up.

170
00:12:27,825 --> 00:12:28,745
Tao.

171
00:12:29,585 --> 00:12:30,425
You've changed a lot.

172
00:12:30,505 --> 00:12:32,025
You've become more mature.

173
00:12:33,345 --> 00:12:35,025
If I hadn't changed,

174
00:12:35,105 --> 00:12:37,785
these past few years
would've been for nothing.

175
00:12:40,345 --> 00:12:43,265
The man just now, that Luke, is your boss?

176
00:12:44,825 --> 00:12:46,305
He doesn't look easy to get along with.

177
00:12:48,185 --> 00:12:49,865
Just don't get on his bad side.

178
00:12:50,385 --> 00:12:53,065
Looks like you're doing
pretty well at work, Tao.

179
00:13:02,545 --> 00:13:03,745
Well…

180
00:13:05,705 --> 00:13:06,745
It's been tough.

181
00:13:09,185 --> 00:13:10,025
I know

182
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:13,865
it wasn't easy for you to stick it out
in Beijing all these years.

183
00:13:13,945 --> 00:13:16,305
Back then, you wanted to go north,
and I wanted to come south.

184
00:13:17,225 --> 00:13:18,665
We all knew Beijing wasn't an easy place.

185
00:13:19,705 --> 00:13:20,785
But you were set on it.

186
00:13:20,865 --> 00:13:22,185
I couldn't stop you.

187
00:13:22,905 --> 00:13:24,585
All I could do was wish you the best

188
00:13:24,665 --> 00:13:26,865
and hope this cruel world
wouldn't swallow you whole.

189
00:13:28,025 --> 00:13:29,545
Sometimes I wonder

190
00:13:31,065 --> 00:13:34,065
if I hadn't come to Shenzhen
and had gone to Beijing with you instead,

191
00:13:34,785 --> 00:13:36,745
would I have made it this far too?

192
00:13:43,745 --> 00:13:45,385
Yao Bei told me

193
00:13:45,465 --> 00:13:47,785
you've made lots of new friends
in Beijing.

194
00:13:48,625 --> 00:13:51,585
Work's been going well,
you got promoted, got a raise,

195
00:13:51,665 --> 00:13:54,625
and even landed a major project
all on your own.

196
00:13:55,145 --> 00:13:56,305
I'm really proud of you.

197
00:14:01,185 --> 00:14:03,385
It was my fault.
I didn't hold on hard enough,

198
00:14:03,905 --> 00:14:05,825
so you had to carry all that on your own.

199
00:14:12,145 --> 00:14:13,145
Let's not talk about that.

200
00:14:14,905 --> 00:14:16,265
It's my first time in Shenzhen.

201
00:14:16,345 --> 00:14:17,985
The sea is beautiful.

202
00:14:21,305 --> 00:14:22,465
Do you like it here?

203
00:14:23,425 --> 00:14:25,545
I bought a two-bedroom apartment nearby.

204
00:14:26,065 --> 00:14:28,465
On weekends, I bring my parents over.

205
00:14:29,265 --> 00:14:31,985
They like going to the market
in the morning to buy fresh seafood.

206
00:14:32,065 --> 00:14:35,145
In the evening, we'll stroll along
the beach and watch the sunset.

207
00:14:36,545 --> 00:14:38,385
If you have time while you're here,

208
00:14:38,465 --> 00:14:39,785
I can show you around.

209
00:14:42,545 --> 00:14:43,625
Nice.

210
00:14:45,505 --> 00:14:47,465
Isn't this the life you've always wanted?

211
00:14:47,545 --> 00:14:50,105
Congrats. I'm really happy for you.

212
00:15:06,865 --> 00:15:07,705
Tao.

213
00:15:09,745 --> 00:15:11,265
I bought your favorite ice cream.

214
00:15:12,305 --> 00:15:13,745
Your favorite, red bean flavor.

215
00:15:18,905 --> 00:15:19,985
Thank you.

216
00:15:20,505 --> 00:15:21,945
Get some rest.

217
00:15:22,025 --> 00:15:23,865
I'll pick you up tomorrow evening.

218
00:15:23,945 --> 00:15:26,265
You can't miss the class reunion.

219
00:15:26,345 --> 00:15:27,225
Xin Zhaozhou,

220
00:15:28,225 --> 00:15:30,545
I have a business dinner tomorrow.

221
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,345
I'm not sure when it ends.

222
00:15:34,025 --> 00:15:35,265
I probably can't make it.

223
00:15:37,305 --> 00:15:39,065
Is it because of me?

224
00:15:45,025 --> 00:15:46,745
Of course not. How could it be?

225
00:15:49,945 --> 00:15:51,545
You haven't changed at all, really.

226
00:15:52,185 --> 00:15:53,425
You're still just as bad at lying.

227
00:15:54,705 --> 00:15:57,425
Whenever you lie,
you can't look me in the eye.

228
00:16:01,825 --> 00:16:02,825
Who says I can't?

229
00:16:06,905 --> 00:16:07,905
Xin Zhaozhou,

230
00:16:09,505 --> 00:16:12,305
I'm really happy I got to see you today.

231
00:16:14,305 --> 00:16:16,545
I've wanted to tell you this
for a long time.

232
00:16:17,905 --> 00:16:20,225
I've never regretted being with you.

233
00:16:20,945 --> 00:16:22,385
I remember

234
00:16:22,465 --> 00:16:25,145
I used to blame you for not going
to Beijing with me.

235
00:16:25,225 --> 00:16:27,985
Looking back now, I honestly think

236
00:16:29,305 --> 00:16:31,305
I was so young and so immature.

237
00:16:32,385 --> 00:16:37,145
But seeing us both today
living the lives we wanted, I think

238
00:16:39,345 --> 00:16:40,545
it's a perfect ending.

239
00:16:40,625 --> 00:16:41,665
I'm happy for us.

240
00:16:47,105 --> 00:16:48,945
I know. I understand.

241
00:16:51,545 --> 00:16:53,225
The past is in the past.

242
00:16:56,145 --> 00:16:58,705
Can I… Can I have one more hug?

243
00:17:01,305 --> 00:17:02,465
Of course.

244
00:17:34,625 --> 00:17:36,465
I hope all my hard work pays off

245
00:17:36,545 --> 00:17:38,625
and that I can become your client soon

246
00:17:39,385 --> 00:17:40,825
and specifically ask for you.

247
00:17:46,185 --> 00:17:47,145
Sure.

248
00:17:47,225 --> 00:17:48,665
That day will come.

249
00:17:50,785 --> 00:17:51,945
I'm leaving.

250
00:18:30,225 --> 00:18:33,665
This is my friend, Xin Zhaozhou.

251
00:18:33,745 --> 00:18:35,145
We're having dinner tonight.

252
00:18:35,945 --> 00:18:36,865
He's also my ex-boyfriend.

253
00:19:41,665 --> 00:19:44,145
What is it, Flora?

254
00:19:45,265 --> 00:19:46,825
You said

255
00:19:46,905 --> 00:19:49,025
we should do one more rehearsal
before tomorrow's client meeting.

256
00:19:49,105 --> 00:19:50,785
I'm here to run through it with you.

257
00:19:52,705 --> 00:19:53,865
Did I?

258
00:19:54,665 --> 00:19:57,385
You said we always rehearse
before an S-tier client workshop.

259
00:20:01,185 --> 00:20:02,225
Come in.

260
00:20:21,425 --> 00:20:22,585
Aren't we rehearsing now?

261
00:20:22,665 --> 00:20:23,745
Go ahead.

262
00:20:24,345 --> 00:20:25,465
Alright.

263
00:20:25,545 --> 00:20:27,825
I'll start then.

264
00:20:28,545 --> 00:20:29,985
We'll begin with the first section.

265
00:20:31,065 --> 00:20:32,225
We…

266
00:20:38,425 --> 00:20:39,665
Can you hear me if I speak like this?

267
00:20:40,665 --> 00:20:42,425
I can. Go ahead.

268
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:48,385
Then I'll start with the first section.

269
00:20:48,465 --> 00:20:50,025
Do you need the laptop?

270
00:20:51,225 --> 00:20:52,425
Do I?

271
00:20:56,185 --> 00:20:58,505
Well, I'll start from my side.

272
00:21:13,865 --> 00:21:14,705
LUAN SIYUAN

273
00:21:17,985 --> 00:21:19,025
Hello?

274
00:21:19,545 --> 00:21:20,865
I'm downstairs at your hotel.

275
00:21:22,225 --> 00:21:23,065
You're here?

276
00:21:24,025 --> 00:21:24,865
I'll be right down.

277
00:21:29,065 --> 00:21:30,545
Practice by yourself.

278
00:21:30,625 --> 00:21:31,665
I'm going out for dinner.

279
00:21:32,945 --> 00:21:33,905
Dinner?

280
00:21:35,305 --> 00:21:36,145
Is it important?

281
00:21:37,825 --> 00:21:39,185
My ex-girlfriend.

282
00:22:08,465 --> 00:22:10,425
If you don't perform well tomorrow,

283
00:22:10,505 --> 00:22:12,745
I'll transfer you to the Shenzhen branch

284
00:22:13,585 --> 00:22:16,225
so that you can rekindle feelings
with your ex-boyfriend.

285
00:22:20,345 --> 00:22:21,225
Luke.

286
00:22:22,505 --> 00:22:24,345
If you can't say anything nice,
don't say anything at all.

287
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:45,745
Luan Nian.

288
00:22:47,705 --> 00:22:49,105
Where are we going, my little brother?

289
00:22:51,025 --> 00:22:52,105
Don't call me that.

290
00:22:52,185 --> 00:22:53,105
-Then what should I call you?
-Excuse me?

291
00:22:53,185 --> 00:22:54,385
My key card has been demagnetized.

292
00:22:54,465 --> 00:22:55,585
Sure. One moment, please.

293
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:58,185
You're on my turf now.
Still want to pick a fight with me?

294
00:23:06,785 --> 00:23:07,945
Let's go.

295
00:23:24,265 --> 00:23:26,625
What's wrong? Trouble at work?

296
00:23:28,425 --> 00:23:29,425
No.

297
00:23:30,385 --> 00:23:34,145
Why do you look
like a rooster that just lost a fight?

298
00:23:37,385 --> 00:23:38,665
What got to you?

299
00:23:40,025 --> 00:23:40,905
Heartbroken?

300
00:23:46,025 --> 00:23:47,145
Siyuan.

301
00:23:48,425 --> 00:23:49,705
Do I really say awful things?

302
00:23:52,745 --> 00:23:55,705
Where's my arrogant little brother?

303
00:23:55,785 --> 00:23:57,785
What happened to my cocky little brother

304
00:23:57,865 --> 00:24:00,905
who could shut anyone up
with his sharp tongue?

305
00:24:00,985 --> 00:24:02,345
What's wrong with you, Luan Siyuan?

306
00:24:04,025 --> 00:24:05,825
You may have the sharpest mouth,

307
00:24:06,825 --> 00:24:09,865
but you've also got the softest heart.

308
00:24:12,185 --> 00:24:13,145
Come on.

309
00:24:13,225 --> 00:24:15,345
I'll treat you to something good.
Let's go.

310
00:24:22,945 --> 00:24:27,145
Today I'll be presenting
the marketing proposal for Jinyuan Tea.

311
00:24:27,705 --> 00:24:30,745
Our overall strategy
is to target younger consumers

312
00:24:30,825 --> 00:24:31,865
while expanding into lower-tier markets.

313
00:24:31,945 --> 00:24:34,585
Based on our market research and analysis,

314
00:24:34,665 --> 00:24:36,065
we've identified
our product's biggest strength.

315
00:24:36,745 --> 00:24:40,065
That is its rarity.

316
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:42,265
It fills a gap in the tea market.

317
00:24:59,305 --> 00:25:01,345
JINYUAN'S BRAND APPROACH
DIFFERENTIATING CHANNELS, CUSTOMIZING

318
00:25:08,265 --> 00:25:11,945
The reason I ran this hiring experiment
was to prove one thing.

319
00:25:12,025 --> 00:25:13,905
People with natural talent
may shine quickly,

320
00:25:13,985 --> 00:25:15,785
but those who keep working hard

321
00:25:15,865 --> 00:25:17,305
are the ones who'll surprise you
in the long run.

322
00:25:17,385 --> 00:25:19,465
Flora was my first test case.

323
00:25:19,545 --> 00:25:21,105
I believe she'll go places.

324
00:25:21,865 --> 00:25:25,545
Maybe not today,
but maybe tomorrow or the day after.

325
00:25:26,065 --> 00:25:27,305
We just have to give her the chance.

326
00:25:31,665 --> 00:25:33,905
Alright. That's all for today.
Thank you, everyone.

327
00:25:41,625 --> 00:25:44,745
Mr. Luan, you've got quite a team.

328
00:25:46,465 --> 00:25:48,305
Luke, here's to you.

329
00:25:48,385 --> 00:25:49,705
Let's have one together.

330
00:25:49,785 --> 00:25:50,945
Cheers.

331
00:25:53,305 --> 00:25:55,625
It's been a real pleasure
working with you.

332
00:25:55,705 --> 00:25:57,145
I hope we can keep working together.

333
00:25:57,225 --> 00:25:58,265
Sure.

334
00:25:58,945 --> 00:26:00,105
Luke.

335
00:26:01,505 --> 00:26:02,465
Flora.

336
00:26:02,545 --> 00:26:04,185
Welcome to Shenzhen.

337
00:26:04,265 --> 00:26:07,905
I'm so happy to have entrusted
this project to Lime.

338
00:26:08,625 --> 00:26:10,345
Your proposal was on point.

339
00:26:10,425 --> 00:26:12,985
It solved most of our problems.
Thank you so much.

340
00:26:13,065 --> 00:26:14,985
Mr. Chen, let me toast you.

341
00:26:15,065 --> 00:26:16,745
We'll definitely make this a hit.

342
00:26:16,825 --> 00:26:18,345
I'll go over the remaining details
with you later.

343
00:26:19,505 --> 00:26:21,265
-Sure.
-Thanks for your support.

344
00:26:21,345 --> 00:26:22,705
Looking forward to working together again.

345
00:26:26,105 --> 00:26:27,065
Flora.

346
00:26:29,465 --> 00:26:30,665
-We'll talk later.
-Okay.

347
00:26:30,745 --> 00:26:31,865
Thanks.

348
00:26:34,665 --> 00:26:37,185
-Mr. Luan, a toast to you. Thank you.
-Flora, well done today.

349
00:26:41,385 --> 00:26:43,305
Flora, you were amazing today.

350
00:26:44,625 --> 00:26:46,425
-You did an incredible job.
-Thank you.

351
00:26:51,385 --> 00:26:53,545
Actually, I don't handle alcohol
very well.

352
00:27:07,865 --> 00:27:08,905
Flora.

353
00:27:36,705 --> 00:27:37,585
I'm fine.

354
00:27:38,545 --> 00:27:40,425
-I'm okay.
-Come. Lie down.

355
00:28:00,865 --> 00:28:02,785
XIN ZHAOZHOU

356
00:28:17,025 --> 00:28:18,065
Hi.

357
00:28:18,145 --> 00:28:20,785
We're having our class reunion tonight.
I can't get hold of Shang Zhitao.

358
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:21,905
I'm a little worried,
so I came to check on her.

359
00:28:23,745 --> 00:28:25,425
She drank too much.
She's lying on the bed.

360
00:28:25,505 --> 00:28:26,745
She might throw up soon.

361
00:28:27,985 --> 00:28:29,105
Tao.

362
00:28:30,745 --> 00:28:31,905
Easy, Tao.

363
00:28:42,105 --> 00:28:43,185
Get it all out. Rinse your mouth.

364
00:28:49,105 --> 00:28:49,985
Now lie back down.

365
00:28:58,985 --> 00:29:00,225
I'll stay and take care of her tonight.

366
00:29:01,185 --> 00:29:02,025
Sounds good.

367
00:29:02,545 --> 00:29:04,905
Since you're here,
that saves me the trouble.

368
00:29:09,265 --> 00:29:10,785
Thanks for bringing her back.

369
00:29:10,865 --> 00:29:13,265
I'll look after her.
You should head back and get some rest.

370
00:29:14,985 --> 00:29:15,865
I can't do that.

371
00:29:16,745 --> 00:29:18,265
I'm responsible for the safety
of my company's female employees.

372
00:29:19,385 --> 00:29:22,825
Leaving a drunk woman alone with a man
is a bit risky.

373
00:29:24,505 --> 00:29:26,345
-We are actually…
-You're her ex, right?

374
00:29:26,425 --> 00:29:27,385
I know.

375
00:29:28,905 --> 00:29:30,825
Ex. Not current.

376
00:29:34,985 --> 00:29:35,905
Go ahead and take care of her.

377
00:29:36,625 --> 00:29:38,225
I'll be here. I won't get in your way.

378
00:29:40,385 --> 00:29:41,545
Luan Nian…

379
00:29:41,625 --> 00:29:43,065
Luan Nian…

380
00:29:43,145 --> 00:29:44,385
You…

381
00:29:44,465 --> 00:29:45,945
You jerk.

382
00:29:46,745 --> 00:29:48,585
You're a real piece of work.

383
00:29:49,865 --> 00:29:50,905
Who's Luan Nian?

384
00:29:53,265 --> 00:29:54,305
No idea.

385
00:29:55,385 --> 00:29:57,545
Maybe some guy she has a crush on.

386
00:29:58,985 --> 00:30:00,145
I want water.

387
00:30:01,105 --> 00:30:02,425
I want water.

388
00:30:13,745 --> 00:30:14,905
Drink slowly.

389
00:30:25,225 --> 00:30:26,265
You're not leaving?

390
00:30:26,345 --> 00:30:27,945
You're not gone either.

391
00:30:32,225 --> 00:30:33,625
Tao can't hold her liquor.

392
00:30:33,705 --> 00:30:34,585
And she threw up so much.

393
00:30:35,185 --> 00:30:36,825
Her throat's going to hurt later tonight.

394
00:30:37,425 --> 00:30:38,785
Whenever she's sick,
she kicks the blanket off.

395
00:30:40,265 --> 00:30:42,585
She's in safe hands with me. Don't worry.

396
00:30:42,665 --> 00:30:44,425
You're the one who worries me.

397
00:32:26,225 --> 00:32:27,265
Tao!

398
00:32:28,785 --> 00:32:29,825
Bei.

399
00:32:34,785 --> 00:32:36,425
The char siu

400
00:32:37,265 --> 00:32:40,225
and roast goose here are amazing.

401
00:32:40,305 --> 00:32:41,585
They're all my favorites.

402
00:32:41,665 --> 00:32:42,665
Let me try.

403
00:32:42,745 --> 00:32:44,425
The food here is really authentic.

404
00:32:45,545 --> 00:32:46,545
Is it good?

405
00:32:47,065 --> 00:32:47,945
Yes.

406
00:32:48,625 --> 00:32:49,665
Try this.

407
00:32:50,185 --> 00:32:51,265
Thanks.

408
00:32:52,025 --> 00:32:53,705
Let me have a good look at you.

409
00:32:55,665 --> 00:32:58,025
You're much more mature
than when you first went to Beijing.

410
00:32:58,105 --> 00:32:59,025
You're even prettier.

411
00:32:59,625 --> 00:33:01,145
You look great too.

412
00:33:03,705 --> 00:33:04,825
I got married.

413
00:33:07,665 --> 00:33:09,545
What? When did that happen?

414
00:33:09,625 --> 00:33:11,105
Why didn't you tell me?

415
00:33:11,185 --> 00:33:13,865
Two months ago.
It all happened so suddenly.

416
00:33:13,945 --> 00:33:16,545
We didn't have a wedding.
We just registered our marriage.

417
00:33:16,625 --> 00:33:17,865
So we didn't tell many people.

418
00:33:19,465 --> 00:33:21,665
That's wonderful.
What does your husband do?

419
00:33:22,465 --> 00:33:25,065
He's a local. He's an architect.

420
00:33:26,185 --> 00:33:29,825
Back then, he held out the blueprints
he designed and proposed to me

421
00:33:31,265 --> 00:33:33,385
and said I was the client of his life.

422
00:33:34,985 --> 00:33:37,025
For the first time,

423
00:33:37,665 --> 00:33:41,065
I felt the security
of having a family of my own.

424
00:33:42,745 --> 00:33:44,945
I felt incredibly lucky.

425
00:33:46,585 --> 00:33:47,625
Bei,

426
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:51,785
being far from home,
you've found someone so wonderful.

427
00:33:51,865 --> 00:33:53,505
I'm really happy for you.

428
00:33:54,185 --> 00:33:55,345
Thank you.

429
00:34:00,185 --> 00:34:01,585
What about you?

430
00:34:01,665 --> 00:34:02,985
Do you have a boyfriend?

431
00:34:04,665 --> 00:34:05,665
Bei,

432
00:34:06,385 --> 00:34:07,825
you know me.

433
00:34:07,905 --> 00:34:12,025
Relationships have never been
a big part of my life.

434
00:34:15,905 --> 00:34:19,625
Have you thought about Xin Zhaozhou again?

435
00:34:20,425 --> 00:34:21,945
You two just met, didn't you?

436
00:34:22,665 --> 00:34:24,225
You know each other so well.

437
00:34:24,304 --> 00:34:26,304
He's doing really well now.

438
00:34:26,385 --> 00:34:28,545
He'd make a great husband.

439
00:34:29,625 --> 00:34:32,744
At the very least,
he always treated you like a princess,

440
00:34:32,824 --> 00:34:33,905
didn't he?

441
00:34:36,225 --> 00:34:37,744
Actually, I have a boyfriend.

442
00:34:38,545 --> 00:34:40,824
We've been together for four years.

443
00:34:43,145 --> 00:34:47,344
You know, to me,
you've always been such a wonderful girl.

444
00:34:47,425 --> 00:34:50,585
You've been with someone for four years,
yet I've never heard a word about him.

445
00:34:56,505 --> 00:34:58,585
Tao, listen to me.

446
00:34:59,585 --> 00:35:01,825
A good relationship helps you grow.

447
00:35:02,345 --> 00:35:03,865
Once you've dated for over three years,

448
00:35:04,465 --> 00:35:06,425
the chances of getting married
fall sharply.

449
00:35:07,785 --> 00:35:10,865
If you think he's the right man,

450
00:35:10,945 --> 00:35:12,945
you should start thinking
about the future.

451
00:35:13,465 --> 00:35:16,545
After all, a woman needs stability.

452
00:35:17,585 --> 00:35:18,825
Think about yourself too.

453
00:35:27,425 --> 00:35:28,785
Come on. Eat.

454
00:35:28,865 --> 00:35:30,265
Try this.

455
00:35:32,545 --> 00:35:34,145
-Have some more.
-Okay.

456
00:35:35,025 --> 00:35:36,065
Have one too, Bei.

457
00:35:42,705 --> 00:35:46,185
PRE-WEDDING TRAVEL PHOTOSHOOT

458
00:35:54,185 --> 00:35:56,425
Luan Nian, let's take a walk.

459
00:35:56,505 --> 00:35:57,865
I want to talk to you.

460
00:35:59,265 --> 00:36:00,225
Okay.

461
00:36:16,665 --> 00:36:17,505
Luan Nian,

462
00:36:18,905 --> 00:36:19,825
you know,

463
00:36:21,545 --> 00:36:23,505
I have a bucket list.

464
00:36:27,945 --> 00:36:31,265
There's one thing I wanted to do
before I turn 30.

465
00:36:33,345 --> 00:36:36,625
If I meet the right person,

466
00:36:38,185 --> 00:36:39,385
I want to get married.

467
00:36:40,905 --> 00:36:43,265
What if… I mean, what if

468
00:36:45,065 --> 00:36:46,825
we made our relationship public?

469
00:36:48,345 --> 00:36:49,825
We could be together openly.

470
00:36:49,905 --> 00:36:51,105
What do you think?

471
00:36:54,225 --> 00:36:56,185
You seem to like Luke too.

472
00:36:56,265 --> 00:36:57,385
We could raise him.

473
00:36:57,985 --> 00:37:01,865
We could go shopping, watch movies,

474
00:37:01,945 --> 00:37:03,825
meet each other's parents.

475
00:37:03,905 --> 00:37:05,505
We could get married.

476
00:37:05,585 --> 00:37:09,865
And maybe have a child.

477
00:37:10,465 --> 00:37:12,385
Just like a normal couple.

478
00:37:25,025 --> 00:37:26,185
I've never thought about any of that.

479
00:37:27,745 --> 00:37:29,385
I don't have a bucket list.

480
00:37:31,585 --> 00:37:32,585
Shang Zhitao,

481
00:37:34,785 --> 00:37:36,545
I know being with me hasn't been easy.

482
00:37:38,265 --> 00:37:40,345
People around me all say
I'm hard to get along with.

483
00:37:40,425 --> 00:37:41,745
That I've got a terrible temper.

484
00:37:43,145 --> 00:37:45,185
I know I'm not good at loving someone,

485
00:37:45,265 --> 00:37:46,865
but you're still young.

486
00:37:46,945 --> 00:37:48,265
You're not sure about a lot of things.

487
00:37:50,025 --> 00:37:52,185
You say you want to be with me,

488
00:37:52,265 --> 00:37:54,265
yet you still went to a matchmaking event.

489
00:37:56,425 --> 00:37:59,865
When I saw your ex-boyfriend
taking good care of you,

490
00:38:01,585 --> 00:38:05,065
and your roommate acting so close to you,

491
00:38:13,345 --> 00:38:15,465
I realized the kind of life you want

492
00:38:16,785 --> 00:38:18,105
might not be one I can give you.

493
00:38:20,705 --> 00:38:21,665
Luan Nian,

494
00:38:23,625 --> 00:38:25,585
I'm not someone
who falls in love casually.

495
00:38:27,425 --> 00:38:28,825
Before you,

496
00:38:30,185 --> 00:38:32,145
I'd only had one boyfriend.

497
00:38:33,785 --> 00:38:35,745
I never imagined we'd start like this,

498
00:38:35,825 --> 00:38:38,425
but that's how we did.

499
00:38:39,785 --> 00:38:42,825
Plus, you're my boss. My superior.

500
00:38:43,945 --> 00:38:45,945
I need this respectable job.

501
00:38:46,465 --> 00:38:48,225
So I'm exhausted.

502
00:38:49,225 --> 00:38:50,465
But that's on me.

503
00:38:52,745 --> 00:38:53,825
I hope you'll calm down.

504
00:38:59,745 --> 00:39:00,745
Fine.

505
00:39:02,825 --> 00:39:03,905
I get it.

506
00:39:04,745 --> 00:39:07,785
I thought our fourth year together

507
00:39:11,105 --> 00:39:13,625
would mean something deeper
than when we first dated.

508
00:39:29,185 --> 00:39:30,505
To be honest,

509
00:39:31,305 --> 00:39:34,425
what Luan Nian said that day
was sincere and gentle.

510
00:39:36,105 --> 00:39:37,345
But his words cut through our relationship

511
00:39:38,425 --> 00:39:40,545
like a knife,

512
00:39:42,745 --> 00:39:44,945
laying the truth bare. It hurt,

513
00:39:45,465 --> 00:39:47,545
but it also made me see things
more clearly.

514
00:39:52,305 --> 00:39:55,545
Some people are simply out of reach.

515
00:39:57,265 --> 00:40:00,545
Some obsessions have to end.

516
00:40:04,025 --> 00:40:06,345
As much as I longed for love,

517
00:40:07,345 --> 00:40:09,105
I was still struggling with reality.

518
00:40:11,345 --> 00:40:15,665
Between us stood an invisible wall
that neither of us could break through.

519
00:40:16,985 --> 00:40:19,305
It was built from our personalities,
families,

520
00:40:19,385 --> 00:40:21,225
and the way we grew up.

521
00:40:22,665 --> 00:40:24,545
We were never truly
on the same wavelength.

522
00:40:58,745 --> 00:40:59,705
Where were you?

523
00:41:01,225 --> 00:41:03,105
I… I went to see a friend.

524
00:41:03,665 --> 00:41:05,505
I came right back as soon as you called.

525
00:41:06,705 --> 00:41:07,665
Your ex-ex-boyfriend?

526
00:41:12,305 --> 00:41:13,585
I've only had one ex.

527
00:41:13,665 --> 00:41:15,545
Unlike someone
who has a long dating history.

528
00:41:16,545 --> 00:41:18,465
Hello. What's your name?

529
00:41:19,905 --> 00:41:22,305
Hello. You can call me Flora.

530
00:41:22,385 --> 00:41:23,625
I'm Luke's subordinate.

531
00:41:26,585 --> 00:41:27,425
Let's have dinner together.

532
00:41:28,105 --> 00:41:30,265
No thanks. You two go on a date.

533
00:41:31,345 --> 00:41:34,545
Do you think I'd date a man like him?

534
00:41:36,185 --> 00:41:38,625
If he weren't my brother,
I wouldn't even bother with him.

535
00:41:39,745 --> 00:41:41,825
He gets away with everything
just because he's good-looking.

536
00:41:41,905 --> 00:41:43,665
Bad temper. Sharp tongue.

537
00:41:44,385 --> 00:41:47,105
Luan Siyuan, watch your mouth.

538
00:41:50,945 --> 00:41:52,025
Nice to meet you, Miss Luan.

539
00:41:52,985 --> 00:41:56,465
Luke told his colleague
you were his ex-girlfriend.

540
00:41:57,065 --> 00:42:00,105
He even said you were so obedient,
you'd come running whenever he called.

541
00:42:03,305 --> 00:42:06,345
You're really making things up now.

542
00:42:08,865 --> 00:42:09,945
Forget it. I'm not eating with you.

543
00:42:10,025 --> 00:42:11,465
-You can leave now.
-You!

544
00:42:15,345 --> 00:42:16,665
Flora, I'm off.

545
00:42:28,465 --> 00:42:29,585
Do you have a minute?

546
00:42:30,345 --> 00:42:31,305
I

547
00:42:32,505 --> 00:42:33,345
need to talk to you.

548
00:42:37,185 --> 00:42:38,105
Sure.

